  <result aggregation-status="0" type="2">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Output 2.2. Increased capacity of the member States to apply international labour standards</narrative>
   </title>
   <description>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">The UNSDCF, signed on 14 March 2020, recognizes the need for Turkmenistan to address comments of the ILO Supervisory Bodies on par with the recommendations of the UN Treaty Bodies and UPR.

The second National Action Plan on Human Rights (2021-2025) was adopted on 16 April 2021. The performance indicators for the plan contain a separate section concerning ILO issues. This section includes measures to prevent forced labour, which is an issue that has been raised by the ILO Supervisory Bodies for a number of years.
 The ILO consistently advocated for the recognition of ILS and the ILO Supervisory Bodies on par with UN human rights instruments and their supervisory bodies during the development of the UNSDCF and in the UNCT. It also provided comments accordingly to draft CFs.

The ILO consistently advocated for the inclusion of issues of ILO concern into the second NAPHR, and in particular forced labour, especially as the first Action Plan did not. The ILO also provided comments accordingly on drafts of the National Action Plan on Human Rights.</narrative>
   </description>
   <indicator aggregation-status="0" measure="5">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">2.2.2. Percentage of new UN Cooperation Frameworks that include measures to address issues raised by the ILO supervisory bodies</narrative>
    </title>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2020-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2021-12-31"></period-end>
    </period>
   </indicator>
  </result>
  <result aggregation-status="0" type="2">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Output 2.1. Increased capacity of the member States to ratify international labour standards</narrative>
   </title>
   <description>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Turkmenistan ratified C122 on 14 April 2021. The ILO supported the ratification process by making available relevant information and participating in a Government-organised tripartite workshop on C122 in January 2019.</narrative>
   </description>
   <indicator aggregation-status="0" measure="5">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">2.1.1. Number of ratifications of fundamental and governance Conventions or Protocols</narrative>
    </title>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2020-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2021-12-31"></period-end>
    </period>
   </indicator>
  </result>
